Add a block-wide barrier between the two reduction loops in reduceValue.

The first loop only issues SYNC_WARPS, which synchronizes within a warp.
The second loop reads temp[thread+step] across warps, but its SYNC_THREADS
sits at the end of the loop body, so it does not cover the reads performed
by the loop's first iteration. Insert an explicit SYNC_THREADS before the
second loop.

reduceValue is called unconditionally by every thread in the work group,
so the added barrier is reachable by all threads.

--- a/platforms/common/src/kernels/rmsd.cc
+++ b/platforms/common/src/kernels/rmsd.cc
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ DEVICE real reduceValue(real value, LOCAL_ARG volatile real* temp) {
             temp[thread] = temp[thread] + temp[thread+step];
         SYNC_WARPS;
     }
+    SYNC_THREADS;
     for (int step = 32; step < LOCAL_SIZE; step *= 2) {
         if (thread+step < LOCAL_SIZE && thread%(2*step) == 0)
             temp[thread] = temp[thread] + temp[thread+step];
